 "substitutedBy": null,
 "summary": "Defines therapeutic agriculture for the purposes of community gardens as the use of agricultural activities as a means of promoting physical, mental and emotional well-being, rehabilitation and therapy for certain individuals.",
 "title": "Defines therapeutic agriculture for the purposes of community gardens",
 "vetoMessages": {
  "items": [
   {
    "billId": {
     "basePrintNo": "A2185",
     "basePrintNoStr": "A2185-2025",
     "printNo": "A2185",
     "session": 2025,
     "version": ""
    },
    "billPage": 0,
    "chapter": 0,
    "lineEnd": 0,
    "lineStart": 0,
    "memoText": " \n                          VETO MESSAGE - No. 39\n \nTO THE ASSEMBLY:\n \nI am returning herewith, without my approval, the following bill:\n \nAssembly Bill Number 2185, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT  to  amend  the agriculture and markets law, in relation to\n      defining  therapeutic  agriculture  for  purposes   of   community\n      gardens\"\n \n    NOT APPROVED\n \n  This  bill  would  add  a definition of \"therapeutic agriculture\" into\nArticle 2-C of the Agriculture and Markets (AGM) Law regarding community\ngardens.\n \n  I recognize the physical and mental  health  benefits  that  community\ngardening  can  bring, including for individuals with physical or mental\nhealth conditions, disabilities, or other special  needs.  However,  the\ndefinition  of  therapeutic  agriculture proposed in this bill is broad,\nand its impact on existing or future programs is not clear from the bill\ntext. This could lead to unintended consequences and  an  administrative\nburden on the Department of Agriculture and Markets as it implements the\nexisting  community  garden  grants  and  programs.  Current law already\nsufficiently provides for the recognition of health benefits as part  of\nthe Department's community garden programming.\n \n  Therefore, I am constrained to veto this bill.\n \n  The bill is disapproved.                       (signed) KATHY HOCHUL\n \n                               __________\n",
    "signedDate": null,
    "signer": "KATHY HOCHUL",
    "vetoNumber": 39,
    "vetoType": "STANDARD",
    "year": 2025
   }
  ],
